<title>SOUTH AFRICA: JCI yr headline shr, div jumps.</title>
<headline>JCI yr headline shr, div jumps.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		    234	vs 178</p>
<p>    - equity accounted	  457	vs 192</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		     77	 vs 40</p>
<p>    Headline earnings	   349	vs 266</p>
<p>    - gold			  58	 vs 66</p>
<p>    - coal and base metals    101	vs 64</p>
<p>    - chrome			76	 vs 32</p>
<p>    Equity accounted earnings 683	vs 286</p>
<p>    Attrib income		 620	vs 226</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			 748	vs 276</p>
<p>    Tax			     95	 vs 50</p>
<p>Operating and investment income</p>
<p>					406	vs 276</p>
<p>Div payable November 6</p>
<p>on register September 27</p>
<p>Full name: JCI Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'	63	 vs 60</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	   342	vs none</p>
<p>NOTE - Headline earnings represent equity accounted earnings excluding exceptional items and surplus on the realisation of investments and assets.</p>
<p>Directors have resolved to award capitalisation shares to shareholders registered on September 27.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
